        <h2 id="overview">Overview of the Singapore Income Tax System</h2>
        <p>The <strong>Singapore income tax system</strong> is renowned globally for its fairness, administrative simplicity, low headline tax rates, and attractive investment incentives. Administered by the <a href="https://www.iras.gov.sg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline">Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore (IRAS)</a>, Singapore operates on a strict <strong>territorial tax principle</strong>. Under this framework, individuals and corporate entities are generally taxed only on income generated within Singapore or remitted into Singapore under specific statutory conditions.</p>

        <p>Key highlights of taxation in Singapore include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Progressive Personal Rates:</strong> Resident personal income tax rates range from 0% for the first S$20,000 up to 24% for income above S$1,000,000 for Year of Assessment (YA) 2026.</li>
          <li><strong>Flat Corporate Tax Rate:</strong> A headline corporate income tax rate of 17%, supported by generous partial tax exemptions for qualifying new startups and SMEs.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Capital Gains Tax:</strong> No tax on capital gains derived from stock investments, property sales, or cryptocurrency appreciation.</li>
          <li><strong>Single-Tier Corporate Dividend System:</strong> Corporate income is taxed at the company level. Subsequent dividend distributions to shareholders are completely exempt from taxation.</li>
          <li><strong>No Inheritance or Net Wealth Tax:</strong> Estate duty was abolished in 2008, ensuring wealth preservation across generations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="personal-tax-brackets">Singapore Personal Income Tax Brackets 2026</h2>
        <p>Personal income tax in Singapore is levied on a progressive schedule. Taxable income (known as <em>Chargeable Income</em>) is calculated by deducting allowable business/employment expenses and eligible personal tax reliefs from gross income.</p>

        <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="min-w-full border border-hairline text-left text-sm dark:border-overlay-lighter">
