        <h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the Singapore personal income tax rate for 2026?</h3>
            <p>Singapore personal income tax for residents is progressive, starting at 0% for the first S$20,000 of chargeable income and topping out at 24% for income above S$1,000,000.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How are non-residents taxed on income in Singapore?</h3>
            <p>Non-residents are taxed at a flat rate of 15% on employment income or the progressive resident rate, whichever results in a higher tax bill. Non-residents cannot claim personal reliefs.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the corporate tax rate in Singapore?</h3>
